# INV-08 — invented. Five overs for the first side; rain, and the chase cut twice.
# Edge cases: the umpires' figures at the break (four overs, 38 to win, not
# the 46 the first innings would set); a second cut during the chase, between
# overs (three overs, 30 to win); the chase ending on its overs short of the
# revised target, the margin read against that target; the result's
# "(revised target)". The figures are the umpires', typed: no DLS here.
match INV-08
title Rain, a chase cut twice
date 2026-11-08
overs 5
sides Home Away

innings 1 Home
open B1 B2
over BW1  1 1 2 . 4 .
over BW2  6 . 1 1 W:b 2
over BW1  4 1 . 2 1 1
over BW3  . W:c/F10 1 4 2 1
over BW2  2 . 1 6 . 1

innings 2 Away overs=4 target=38
open B1 B2
over BW1  1 4 . 2 1 .
over BW2  W:lbw 1 6 . 1 2
revise overs=3 target=30
over BW3  1 2 . 4 1 1

# ── The card, worked by hand ──
# Home: 8, 10, 9, 8, 10 = 45.
card 1
bat B1 14 11 2 0 c F10 b BW3
bat B2 8 5 0 1 b BW2
bat B3 15 10 1 0 not out
bat B4 8 4 0 1 not out
extras b 0 lb 0 w 0 nb 0 p 0
total 45/2 5.0
fow 1-16 B2 1.5
fow 2-27 B1 3.2
bowl BW1 2-0-17-0 wd 0 nb 0
bowl BW2 2-0-20-1 wd 0 nb 0
bowl BW3 1-0-8-1 wd 0 nb 0

# Away: 8, 10, then 9 in the last of three overs = 27, needing 30.
card 2
bat B1 10 7 0 1 not out
bat B2 7 5 1 0 lbw b BW2
bat B3 10 6 1 0 not out
extras b 0 lb 0 w 0 nb 0 p 0
total 27/1 3.0
fow 1-8 B2 1.1
bowl BW1 1-0-8-0 wd 0 nb 0
bowl BW2 1-0-10-1 wd 0 nb 0
bowl BW3 1-0-9-0 wd 0 nb 0

result Home won by 2 runs (revised target)
